  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "there is/there are: affirmative with prepositions",
      "title_form": "There is / There are con preposiciones de lugar",
      "title_target": "There is / There are with Prepositions of Place",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos **there is** (singular) y **there are** (plural) para decir que algo **existe** o **está en un lugar**. Después de estas expresiones, añadimos una **preposición de lugar** para indicar dónde está la cosa.\n\n- **There is** + un objeto + preposición + lugar.\n- **There are** + varios objetos + preposición + lugar.\n\nEjemplos:\n- `There is a cat under the table.` (Hay un gato debajo de la mesa.)\n- `There are two books on the table.` (Hay dos libros sobre la mesa.)\n\nLa preposición va **después** del objeto, no antes. Esta estructura es muy común para describir una escena o un lugar.",
      "description_md_target": "We use **there is** (singular) and **there are** (plural) to say that something **exists** or **is in a place**. After these expressions, we add a **preposition of place** to indicate where the thing is.\n\n- **There is** + one object + preposition + place.\n- **There are** + several objects + preposition + place.\n\nExamples:\n- `There is a cat under the table.`\n- `There are two books on the table.`\n\nThe preposition goes **after** the object, not before. This structure is very common to describe a scene or a place.",
      "grammar_structure": "There is/are + (a/an) + noun + preposition + place",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "there_is_there_are",
        "headers": [
          "Forma",
          "Uso",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "There is",
            "Un objeto (singular)",
            "There is a cat under the table."
          ],
          [
            "There are",
            "Varios objetos (plural)",
            "There are two books on the table."
          ]
        ]
      },
