  "notes_md_form": "## Preposiciones de lugar: tu mapa mental\n\nPiensa en las preposiciones como un mapa: **on** es contacto con una superficie (the book is on the table), **in** es dentro (the pen is in the bag), **under** es debajo (the cat is under the chair). Para **next to** y **near**, imagina distancia: next to es \"al lado\" (tocando casi), near es \"cerca\" (un poco más lejos). **Between** siempre necesita DOS objetos: the park is between the school and the house.\n\n## Errores comunes\n\n- **No digas \"the book is in the table\"** para \"sobre la mesa\". Usa **on**: the book is on the table.\n- **At vs. in**: at es para un punto exacto (at the door), in es para espacios con límites (in the park).\n- **There is vs. there are**: there is + singular (there is a park near my house), there are + plural (there are two tables in the room). ¡No los confundas!",
